questions.q:
This Xor implementation is missing its last line:

CHIP Xor {
  IN a, b;
  OUT out;
  PARTS:
  Not (in=a, out=nota);
  Not (in=b, out=notb);
  And (a=a, b=notb, out=aAndNotb);
  And (a=nota, b=b, out=notaAndb);
  ???
}

Which line completes it?

Consider:

CHIP AndMuxOr {
  IN a, b, sel;
  OUT out;
  PARTS:
  And (a=a, b=b, out=andOut);
  Or (a=a, b=b, out=orOut);
  Mux (a=andOut, b=orOut, sel=sel, out=out);
}

What is out when a = 1, b = 0, sel = 1? Enter 0 or 1.

Adder3Way adds three 16-bit inputs with two Adder parts:

Adder (a=a, b=b, out=ab);
Adder (a=ab, b=c, out=out);

What is ab?
